<p><strong>The best spa software in Nepal is the one that matches how your spa really runs. It books the therapist and the room together, tracks memberships, packages and gift vouchers, requires approval for discounts and gives you one report across every branch. A single-room studio can start simple. A multi-branch spa needs all of it.</strong></p>
<p>Spa owners in Kathmandu, Lalitpur, Pokhara and beyond now have more choice than ever, from local providers to international products. Choosing on a price list alone usually backfires. Choose on the problems you really have.</p>
<h2>Step 1: Book the therapist and the room together</h2>
<p>A spa booking is not just a time slot. It needs a named therapist, a free room and the right service length, all at once. Software that only holds a diary will still let two guests land in the same room. Look for conflict-free booking across therapists, rooms and branches. See <a href="/features/booking/">how Zennly books</a>.</p>
<h2>Step 2: Check prepaid products</h2>
<p>Most Nepali spas sell <a href="/features/memberships/">memberships</a>, <a href="/features/packages/">session packages</a> and <a href="/features/vouchers/">gift vouchers</a>. The software should track the balance, record each redemption and show what is still owed to the guest. Ask the vendor to show it working, not just listed.</p>
<h2>Step 3: Control discounts and payments</h2>
<p>Staff discounts are where spas quietly lose money. Choose software where a discount is requested, approved and recorded against the booking. Payments should be logged by method, so the daily close is a report rather than an argument. Read about <a href="/features/discount-management/">discount management</a> and <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</p>
<h2>Step 4: Look at staff and payroll</h2>
<p>Therapists move between branches and earn commission. Good spa software handles <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff transfers</a> and <a href="/features/payroll/">payroll with commission and attendance deductions</a>, so month-end is not a spreadsheet exercise.</p>
<h2>Step 5: Compare plainly, then try it</h2>
<p>Use a checklist, not a feeling. Our page on <a href="/compare/spa-salon-software-nepal/">spa and salon software in Nepal, compared</a> lists the questions to put to every vendor. Then <a href="#try-free" data-trial-open>try the free Zennly demo</a> on a working spa setup. For a longer guide, read <a href="/blog/spa-management-software/">spa management software: features and how to choose</a>.</p>
